                <pb facs="0034" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.4061 Motion Pictures/129a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-25T20:00:00-04:00">April 25, 1938—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>172. From Hawkins and Hickerson. We hope to hand the British Trade Delegation
                    tomorrow a draft Trade Agreement. As regards motion pictures, we intend to state
                    that our proposals will be transmitted at a later date. We have discussed the
                    whole question at various times with the British Delegation but in general terms
                    and for the purpose of emphasizing the great importance which we place on
                    satisfactory treatment for this important American industry. We should be glad
                    to have your views regarding the specific proposals on this subject that should
                    be made for inclusion in the Agreement. [Hawkins and Hickerson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
